cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "biofilm-embeddings: DINOv2 vision-transformer embeddings for brightfield biofilm timelapse microscopy"
abstract: >-
  Turns per-well brightfield timelapse image stacks from 96-well plate
  microscopy into frozen DINOv2 vision-transformer embeddings. Each frame is
  described by a CLS token and a pooled 3x3 grid of patch tokens, giving every
  well a trajectory through embedding space for downstream analysis (fPCA, UMAP,
  clustering, path signatures). Image processing is provided by biofilm-processing,
  vendored at a pinned version so the render cannot drift under the embeddings.
  Ships a PySide6 GUI and a headless CLI.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-07-29
repository-code: "https://github.com/melsehna/biofilm-embeddings"
